steps.text:
Use keybindings that pass `logicalLine: true` to the cursor commands:

```json
{
  "key": "ctrl+alt+down",
  "command": "editor.action.insertCursorBelow",
  "args": { "logicalLine": true }
},
{
  "key": "ctrl+alt+up",
  "command": "editor.action.insertCursorAbove",
  "args": { "logicalLine": true }
}
```

This makes “add cursor above/below” move between logical document lines, skipping soft-wrapped display lines—the behavior shown in the second GIF. On macOS, use your preferred `cmd`/`option` equivalents.
